WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.375 --> 00:00:14.703
The weeks leading up to the big event passed like mere minutes and before they could catch their

2
00:00:14.723 --> 00:00:17.646
breath, the eve of Meg's wedding day was upon them.

3
00:00:18.467 --> 00:00:24.091
The girls changed into their pajamas but nobody felt like sleeping because this was the last evening that

4
00:00:24.151 --> 00:00:25.172
Meg would spend with them.

5
00:00:25.192 --> 00:00:31.809
"This time tomorrow, you will be a married woman," Amy stated as she brushed Meg's hair.

6
00:00:31.829 --> 00:00:33.570
"Are you nervous?"

7
00:00:34.030 --> 00:00:36.111
asked Beth, laying her hand over Meg's.

8
00:00:37.091 --> 00:00:38.912
"No," said Meg with a smile.

9
00:00:38.932 --> 00:00:43.654
"After such a long engagement, John and I can't wait to be married."

10
00:00:43.674 --> 00:00:46.836
"Have you already forgotten about us then?"

11
00:00:47.276 --> 00:00:48.596
Jo pouted childishly.

12
00:00:48.616 --> 00:00:55.900
"Of course not, Jo," Meg said gently, extending a hand, which Jo diverted her eyes from and turned

13
00:00:55.940 --> 00:01:00.230
away. "I'm going to miss you girls very much," Meg continued.

14
00:01:00.250 --> 00:01:05.612
"But since I'll live just down the road, I'll expect daily visits so that we'll always remain in

15
00:01:05.672 --> 00:01:06.352
close touch."

16
00:01:07.433 --> 00:01:13.716
The sisters, including Jo, encircled Meg and after many sniffles, cries, and loving words, they went off to

17
00:01:13.756 --> 00:01:20.059
bed. Several hours later as Jo was lying wide awake in the dark, she felt a familiar hand

18
00:01:20.139 --> 00:01:20.799
on her shoulder.

19
00:01:20.819 --> 00:01:26.758
"Jo?" whispered Meg as she slid over to her sister and held Jo's hand as they did when

20
00:01:26.778 --> 00:01:27.599
they were little girls.

21
00:01:27.619 --> 00:01:33.882
"I'm going to miss you, Meg," Jo whispered tearfully.

22
00:01:33.902 --> 00:01:36.324
"Me too," replied Meg.

23
00:01:36.344 --> 00:01:39.085
"Take care of the girls, Jo."

24
00:01:39.966 --> 00:01:44.949
Nodding, Jo squeezed Meg's hand and the two sisters fell asleep side by side.

25
00:01:46.490 --> 00:01:49.852
Meg could not have chosen a more perfect day for the wedding.

26
00:01:51.412 --> 00:01:56.237
The sun was out bright and early while a gentle, light breeze pushed away the heat to make

27
00:01:56.277 --> 00:01:58.599
the temperature ideal for an outdoor ceremony.

28
00:01:59.860 --> 00:02:05.885
Due to their tight budget, Meg and John had planned a small, intimate wedding, inviting only family and

29
00:02:05.905 --> 00:02:06.926
a few close friends.

30
00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:13.292
Among the guests was Sallie Gardiner, Meg's close friend, who had married Ned Moffat a few months before.

31
00:02:14.874 --> 00:02:21.253
Sallie had had a lavish, elegant wedding, but Meg's simple yet warm ceremony was just as memorable.

32
00:02:22.374 --> 00:02:23.634
"Look at your tie, Brookes!

33
00:02:23.994 --> 00:02:27.695
It's a mess," Laurie cried, undoing the tie and re-doing it skillfully.

34
00:02:27.715 --> 00:02:32.337
"Thanks, Laurie, I'm a bit nervous," admitted his former tutor.

35
00:02:32.357 --> 00:02:38.199
"That's understandable, considering today is the most important day of your life!

36
00:02:38.679 --> 00:02:42.580
But everything is going to be fine," reassured his grown-up pupil.

37
00:02:43.648 --> 00:02:48.289
Beth came out wearing a light blue silk dress and pink flowers in her hair.

38
00:02:48.970 --> 00:02:53.411
She sat down at the piano that was brought out especially for the occasion and began playing.

39
00:02:54.651 --> 00:02:59.893
Although Meg had wanted all three of her sisters to be bridesmaids, Beth was too nervous to walk

40
00:02:59.933 --> 00:03:01.833
down the aisle and have everyone stare at her.

41
00:03:02.714 --> 00:03:05.594
Instead, she offered to play the music for the wedding.

42
00:03:06.515 --> 00:03:10.656
Taking her cue, the guests found their seats and waited for the bride to enter.

43
00:03:12.192 --> 00:03:18.157
First Jo and Amy walked in together, each carrying a small bouquet, and wearing identical dresses to Beth's.

44
00:03:19.038 --> 00:03:21.179
The girls smiled as they walked down the aisle.

45
00:03:21.199 --> 00:03:25.763
"She's so beautiful," Laurie murmured as the girls passed him.

46
00:03:27.024 --> 00:03:33.289
"That Amy is going to break many hearts," replied Sallie, thinking Laurie was talking about the youngest March

47
00:03:33.309 --> 00:03:39.735
sister. Laurie, however, was not referring to Amy; his eyes and heart were set on the other sister.

48
00:03:40.815 --> 00:03:43.837
Finally, the bride walked down the aisle with her father.

49
00:03:44.978 --> 00:03:46.939
Meg looked radiant in her white gown.

50
00:03:47.899 --> 00:03:51.882
She wore white daisies in her hair and held a simple bouquet of flowers in her hand.

51
00:03:53.583 --> 00:03:57.805
It was her smile, however, that lit up her face and illuminated her joy.

52
00:03:58.865 --> 00:04:00.126
The ceremony was short.

53
00:04:01.227 --> 00:04:04.689
Once Meg and John had exchanged their vows and rings, Mr.

54
00:04:04.709 --> 00:04:05.089
and Mrs.

55
00:04:05.169 --> 00:04:07.390
Brookes presented themselves to their guests.

56
00:04:07.410 --> 00:04:10.752
"Congratulations to you both!"

57
00:04:11.252 --> 00:04:14.833
Cheers and best wishes for the new couple were heard throughout the reception.

58
00:04:16.714 --> 00:04:22.936
Jo, having endured starvation for as long as her body would permit, could no longer neglect her rumbling

59
00:04:22.996 --> 00:04:27.977
stomach and purposefully made her way to the buffet table to indulge to her heart's content.

60
00:04:28.898 --> 00:04:31.899
Following closely behind like a lovesick puppy was Laurie.

61
00:04:31.919 --> 00:04:36.160
"Jo, you look amazing," he kept saying, much to her annoyance.

62
00:04:37.544 --> 00:04:42.907
"If you wore this dress and put this paint on your face, Laurie," Jo said, indicating her gown

63
00:04:42.967 --> 00:04:45.148
and makeup, "you'd be gorgeous too.

64
00:04:45.629 --> 00:04:47.490
Now, stop embarrassing me and go away."

65
00:04:48.470 --> 00:04:53.673
Laurie was not easily discouraged and would have gone on, if not for the entrance of an uninvited

66
00:04:53.753 --> 00:04:56.274
guest. "Josephine!"

67
00:04:56.695 --> 00:05:03.698
Aunt March's voice shrilled loudly, causing everyone to stop mid-conversation and frightening Beth so that she stopped playing

68
00:05:03.738 --> 00:05:04.219
her music.

69
00:05:05.139 --> 00:05:09.722
Jo nearly dropped her plate because Aunt March was the last person she expected to see.

70
00:05:09.742 --> 00:05:12.043
"Where is she?

71
00:05:12.763 --> 00:05:14.244
Where is your sister?"

72
00:05:15.105 --> 00:05:19.307
Aunt March demanded, briskly walking toward Jo and Laurie with determination.

73
00:05:19.327 --> 00:05:26.911
"I'm here, Aunt March," Meg boldly called out and cautiously approached her aunt, while John followed closely behind.

74
00:05:28.552 --> 00:05:31.334
Aunt March did not speak until Meg stood before her.

75
00:05:32.074 --> 00:05:35.136
When she arrived, the old woman scrutinized her from head to toe.

76
00:05:35.956 --> 00:05:40.059
"Yes, yes, all very simple like you," Aunt March snapped.

77
00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:46.063
John opened his mouth to defend his wife but Meg gently placed her hand on his arm to

78
00:05:46.123 --> 00:05:46.664
silence him.

79
00:05:47.684 --> 00:05:53.048
Since their last encounter, which had ended so disastrously, Meg had not spoken to her aunt for the

80
00:05:53.088 --> 00:05:54.129
past three years.

81
00:05:54.989 --> 00:05:56.571
"What can I do for you, Aunt March?"

82
00:05:56.991 --> 00:05:57.811
Meg asked calmly.

83
00:05:57.831 --> 00:06:04.036
"I've come to give you your wedding gift," Aunt March said, holding out a white envelope.

84
00:06:05.052 --> 00:06:09.894
"Aunt March, it isn't necessary for you to give a gift," Meg said graciously but firmly.

85
00:06:10.635 --> 00:06:16.217
Aunt March peered at Meg, then softening a little she said, "I know I uttered words that I

86
00:06:16.297 --> 00:06:18.998
shouldn't have and I regret them deeply.

87
00:06:20.299 --> 00:06:27.642
You are my only living relatives she choked up but continued, "and I would like nothing more than

88
00:06:27.702 --> 00:06:31.384
to make the best use of my time on earth while I can."

89
00:06:32.276 --> 00:06:38.021
Mrs. Brookes warmly embraced her old aunt and gave her a tender kiss saying, "Thank you, Aunt March,

90
00:06:38.081 --> 00:06:42.265
for helping my husband and me start our married life at peace with our loved ones."

91
00:06:44.266 --> 00:06:48.770
Appropriately, Beth started up the music again and everyone laughed and danced merrily.

92
00:06:48.790 --> 00:06:51.172
"Do you think they'll be happy?"

93
00:06:51.573 --> 00:06:54.855
Jo asked Laurie as they watched her sister and brother-in-law dance.

94
00:06:56.156 --> 00:06:57.758
"Naturally," Laurie replied.

95
00:06:57.778 --> 00:07:00.020
"They are, after all, in love."

96
00:07:01.276 --> 00:07:05.918
Snorting, Jo remarked, "I think love is rather silly."

97
00:07:07.419 --> 00:07:10.060
Laurie held his tongue, but he disagreed.

98
00:07:11.260 --> 00:07:16.142
After hours of celebrating, Meg and John were ready to go to their new home, just down the

99
00:07:16.182 --> 00:07:17.463
street from her family's house.

100
00:07:17.483 --> 00:07:23.685
"Well, here we are," John said, stopping in front of their small modest house.

101
00:07:25.246 --> 00:07:30.028
"It's not as cozy as your place or as grand as the Laurence mansion but it's ours."

102
00:07:30.836 --> 00:07:36.971
Taking his arm in hers, Meg smiled at him and said, "Yes, it's our home, sweet home."
